# fraud-analytics-job/.dockerignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so without this file every path in the
# build context lands in the production job image.
#
# Added 2026-08-14 alongside the GNN work (ADR-0002), which introduced the
# repository's first pytest suite in tests/. Unit tests and their synthetic data
# generator have no business in a production fraud-detection image.
#
# NOTE: docker does NOT read .gitignore. Several entries below are already
# git-ignored, which means they are absent in a clean CI checkout but present in
# a local working tree — so a local `docker build` embeds them while a CI build
# does not. That divergence is exactly what this file removes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Tests (ADR-0002) — must not ship ─────────────────────────────────────────
tests/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fraud-analytics-job/.env exists in local working trees and would otherwise be
# baked into the image at /app/.env. The job reads the repo-root .env (see
# run_job.py: parent.parent / ".env"), which is outside this build context, so
# excluding this changes nothing at runtime in any environment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Build / run artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Output/ holds trained .pkl models and .png charts from local runs. It is
# recreated at runtime by train_fraud_model.py (OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir), so shipping a
# stale local copy is pure weight — and a stale local model in the image would
# be actively confusing during an incident.
Output/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
